      "problem": "If $v=8,$ then $2-\\frac{v}{5}=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Replacing $v$ with $8$ in the expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-\\frac{v}{5} & = \\\\ 2-\\frac{8}{5} & = \\\\ \\frac{2\\cdot 5-8}{5} & = \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
